// AUTO-GENERATED by `npm run measure:holes -- --emit`.
// Do not hand-edit — rerun the script to refresh.
//
// The REAL seating plane of every receiving pin hole, measured from the
// converted GLB meshes: the outermost material in the collar annulus about
// the hole axis — the surface a connector actually lands on. A VEX IQ hole
// sits at the bottom of a moulded pocket, so this is typically ~0.030 INSIDE
// the part's outer skin, which is where the authored metadata used to put it.
//
// `seatOffset` is the signed axial distance from the hole MARKER
// (`mateFrame.position`) along its OUTWARD normal. Negative = recessed into
// the part. Holes absent from this table had no confident ring of material
// near their face and keep their authored face plane.

